       [#D7D7AF][/dim]sase-18t (ToolRun store \"database is locked\" under parallel load), [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]sase-1a7 (the Files ctrl+j anchor-scroll node that keeps Full CI [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]red), sase-12f (the monitor-capacity fakey e2e that exits 124 under[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]load), and sase-1ot (owner-approved rotation and purge of 27 [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]historical secret-scanner hits in public sase--agents history). The[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]land agent then starts the next backlog epic, five beads at a time,[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]until no workable task bead remains.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim] Counts: [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]5[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] phases[dim][/dim] · [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]2[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] waves[/dim]\n[dim]   Path: [#87AFFF][/dim]plan:202610/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]backlog_epic_2_top_five_task_beads.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim] Prompt: [#87AFFF][/dim]prompts/202610/backlog_epic_2_top_five_task_beads.md[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Bead: [#87AFFF][/dim]sase-1ou[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Page: [#87AFFF][/dim]https://github.com/sase-org/sase--beads/blob/main/pages/sase-1ou/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]README.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim]  1 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Make the flake-baseline gate reach a truthful verdict again [/bold #D7AFFF]  [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n      [bold #D7AFFF](sase-1og)[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]flake-baseline[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]flake-baseline: drop the duplicate fixed-at directive that makes [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]tools/selection_health --fail-on-new-flake exit 2, add a regression test[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]that parses the committed baseline, then reconcile the 64 exceedances [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]the unmasked gate reports (fixed-at for verified fixes, baseline entries[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]only under existing open beads, follow-ups for the rest), and close [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]sase-1og.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Stop the ToolRun store failing with \"database is locked\" under[bold white on #D75F87][/bold #D7AFFF] large  [/bold white on #D75F87]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]parallel load (sase-18t)[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]toolrun-busy[dim] · [dim][/dim]after flake-baseline[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]toolrun-busy: identify which sase-core ToolRun store transactions hold [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]the SQLite write lock while launcher, settle and show paths read it, fix[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]the contention at its source in sase-core with a principled busy policy,[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]move the core pin, retire the tests/tool/ baseline entries with [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]fixed-at, and close sase-18t.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Make the weight-two land-agent-session capacity e2e [/bold #D7AFFF]          [bold white on #D75F87] large  [/bold white on #D75F87]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]load-robust (sase-12f)[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]capacity-e2e[dim] · [dim][/dim]after flake-baseline[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]capacity-e2e: find what consumes the fakey land agent's 5 s budget under[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]load in tests/fakey/test_monitor_capacity_e2e.py (delayed child [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]bootstrap, capacity scan under the host-wide slot lock, or harness [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]polling), fix the cause instead of the timeout, prove it with a loaded [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]stress loop, and close sase-12f.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  4 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Fix the Files ctrl+j page-anchor scroll race (sase-1a7)[/bold #D7AFFF]       [bold white on #D75F87] large  [/bold white on #D75F87]\n    [#AF87FF]deck-anchor[dim] · [dim][/dim]after flake-baseline[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]deck-anchor: reproduce the intermittent wait_for_anchor_scroll timeout [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]in t